  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you expand your friend's list, the list is still sorted alphabetically across and down.\nIn other words, you may have five rows of friends arranged like so:\nA-E\nF-J\nK-O\nP-T\nU-Z\nBut this arrangement is annoying, because you can't simply scroll right quickly until you get close to the first letter of the name you're looking for... you instead have to remember to first look down the left side of the list and figure out which row will contain the name based on what letters come before and after the letter you're looking for, and then focus only on the correct row as you quickly scroll across, because our brains weren't designed to scan four or five rows of letters simultaneously and detect when we get close to what we're looking for that way.\nThis would probaby also help guys like Lolathon with 300 avatars find an avatar more quickly if the avatars could be sorted by name instead of creation date.",
